config XIAOMI_MI_SCHEDULE
	tristate "Xiaomi task-state carrier (slots, cluster type, 32B uid map)"
	depends on ARM64 && ANDROID_VENDOR_HOOKS && ANDROID_VENDOR_OEM_DATA
	help
	  Per-task state carrier for the Xiaomi policy modules: mi_task_struct
	  slots in the GKI task tail, cluster typing from the native topology
	  masks, and the 32-bit compat UID map. Fork production attaches to
	  the native android_rvh_sched_fork; free/cleanup to
	  android_vh_free_task. The stock per-UID runtime accounting and
	  /proc/package faces are dropped: 6.18 owns load tracking
	  (PELT/schedstat), and their producers were closed-scheduler calls.
